{"subject": "maths", "level": "ibdp", "topic_display": "Calculus", "topic_slug": "calculus", "theme": "maths-grid", "adventure_n": 1, "title": "Limits and Differentiation Rules", "emoji": "📉", "welcome_lead": "Slice into change with limits and the power, product, quotient and chain rules.", "meta_desc": "Maths adventure on limits and differentiation: power, product, quotient, chain.", "final_note": "Chain rule: outside times derivative of inside!", "concepts": [{"term": "Limit", "def": "lim x→a f(x) = L if f(x) approaches L."}, {"term": "Derivative", "def": "f'(x) = lim h→0 (f(x+h) - f(x))/h."}, {"term": "Power rule", "def": "d/dx (x^n) = n x^(n-1)."}, {"term": "Product rule", "def": "(uv)' = u'v + uv'."}, {"term": "Quotient rule", "def": "(u/v)' = (u'v - uv') / v^2."}, {"term": "Chain rule", "def": "(f(g(x)))' = f'(g(x)) × g'(x)."}], "walkthroughs": [{"tag": "power", "h2": "Power Rule", "body_html": "<p>Differentiate f(x) = 3x^4.</p><p>f'(x) = 3 × 4 x^3 = 12x^3.</p>"}, {"tag": "chain", "h2": "Chain Rule", "body_html": "<p>Differentiate y = sin(3x^2).</p><p>dy/dx = cos(3x^2) × 6x = 6x cos(3x^2).</p>"}, {"tag": "product", "h2": "Product Rule", "body_html": "<p>Differentiate y = x^2 e^x.</p><p>dy/dx = 2x e^x + x^2 e^x = e^x (2x + x^2).</p>"}], "mcqs": [{"q": "d/dx of x^5?", "options": [["5x^4", 1], ["x^4", 0], ["5x^5", 0], ["4x^5", 0]]}, {"q": "d/dx of ln(x)?", "options": [["1/x", 1], ["x", 0], ["e^x", 0], ["-1/x^2", 0]]}], "numericals": [{"q": "Derivative of x^3 at x = 2?", "options": [6, 8, 12, 24], "answer": 12}], "free_texts": [{"q": "Rule for composite functions?", "answer": "chain rule"}]}